Falsifies `calendar::verification::parse_is_total_on_hostile_bytes`.

The defect: `parse_rfc3339_bytes` loses the check that the offset designator exists. A 20-byte input whose
fraction runs to the last byte leaves `i` at the end of the slice and `b[i]` reads past it.
(Removing the length guard inside `number` instead stays green: every call to `number` is already
bounded by an earlier check, so that guard is defence in depth that no input reaches.)

Expected to fail: the bounds check on `b[i]` in `parse_rfc3339_bytes`.

